  "id": "COMPOUND:17902 - PROTEIN:6231",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between (Z)-4-Methoxy-3,3',5,5'-tetrahydroxystilbene and Histone-lysine N-methyltransferase, H3 lysine-9 specific 5. This compound is identified as a target of multiple molecules, including EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, Kuhlmannin, and 2-Carbomethoxy-9,10-anthraquinone, all of which are known to interact with histone methyltransferases. The shared target of these molecules points to a potential mechanism where (Z)-4-Methoxy-3,3',5,5'-tetrahydroxystilbene may inhibit the activity of the H3 lysine-9 specific methyltransferase, thereby affecting chromatin structure and function. The consistent presence of this compound as a target across different pathways supports the hypothesis that it acts through a common biological mechanism, likely involving the inhibition of histone methyltransferase activity. The evidence is robust and aligns with the expected role of such compounds in modulating epigenetic regulation.",
